{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1791148116,"nonce":"5JoSb2NgieAa2Hs9z/z9sDzCerQ=","message":"The multi-run path is fixed too, and the spacing problem that blocked it is solved.\n\nEach run is now sized to its DRAWN text, with its edge spaces spent on position instead of left inside the box. Text rendering drops a leading or trailing space, so a box that merely reserved room for one came out butted against its neighbour. The run is placed at x_cursor + the leading space's width, sized to the trimmed text, and x_cursor still advances by the full width including spaces.\n\nVerified by instrumenting the geometry: 'Inline marks: bold, italic, strikethrough,' draws 234.05 wide and advances 236.40, so the 2.35px space is real and the following code run starts after it.\n\nAn offscreen harness for this, examples/rte_capture.rs, renders the editor through BlincApp::render_to_rgba8. The windowed demo needs a screen grab and is not deterministic; this made the iteration possible.\n\nSeparate defect seen while fixing this, not yet filed: the strikethrough decoration is drawn across the whole run box rather than only its span, so it extends past 'strikethrough,' and visually closes the gap before the following code run.","files":null}]}